### Did the FBI take possession of a laptop computer that was identified as belonging to Hunter Biden?
Answer: Yes, according to multiple senior administration officials who spoke to Fox News in October 2020, "The FBI is in possession of the laptop purportedly belonging to Hunter Biden." This is further corroborated by FBI paperwork detailing "serial numbers for a laptop and hard drive taken into possession."

Source URL: https://www.foxnews.com/politics/fbi-purported-hunter-biden-laptop-sources

### On what date did the FBI first take possession of the laptop computer in question?
Answer: Based on the search result, the FBI first took possession of the laptop computer on December 9, 2019, as indicated by a subpoena issued to the repair shop owner on that date which details serial numbers for the devices taken into custody.

Source URL: https://news.yahoo.com/hunter-biden-purported-laptop-connected-120252142.html

### What was the documented chain of custody for the laptop computer from the time it left Hunter Biden's possession until it was received by the FBI?
Answer: The documented chain of custody indicates the laptop was dropped off at a Delaware repair shop in April 2019 and never retrieved; the shop owner, John Paul Mac Isaac, later reported it to authorities, and the FBI subsequently subpoenaed the laptop and hard drive in December 2019 as part of a money laundering investigation.

Source URL: https://news.yahoo.com/hunter-biden-purported-laptop-connected-120252142.html

