### Justification
The fact-check establishes that a laptop belonging to Hunter Biden was left at a Delaware repair shop in April 2019, with a signed document confirming its ownership. The FBI took possession of the laptop and a hard drive via a legal subpoena issued on December 9, 2019, in connection with a money laundering investigation, as detailed in FBI paperwork and reported by [Fox News](https://www.foxnews.com/politics/fbi-purported-hunter-biden-laptop-sources) and [Yahoo News](https://news.yahoo.com/hunter-biden-purported-laptop-connected-120252142.html). While the FBI did not issue an official public confirmation prior to the claim date, multiple sources—including senior administration officials and the documented subpoena—corroborate the agency's possession, supporting the claim.